digraph ReasoningTree {
  rankdir="TB";
  "I10" [label="(0,0,0) Abduction: Given phase transformation mechanism for grain refinement is unclear, new characterization methods are needed to understand the mechanism"];
  "I11" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction: If understanding composition-property relationships enables targeted compositions and targeted compositions enhance performance, then deeper understanding leads to better AM components"];
  "I4" [label="(0,0,0) Induction: Multiple successful strategies exist for grain refinement, therefore composition manipulation is a viable approach for grain control"];
  "I5" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction: If secondary phases pin boundaries and break epitaxial growth, then introducing secondary phases can refine grains"];
  "N13" [label="(10,23,16) High cooling rates and thermal gradient in AM enable microstructural refinement at nanoscale"];
  "N14" [label="(8,1,0) Composition has potential to alter microstructures in AM"];
  "N15" [label="(10,1,0) Successful strategies for grain refinement include combining pre-existing alloys"];
  "N16" [label="(10,3,0) Decorating powder feedstock with nucleant particles is a successful grain refinement strategy"];
  "N17" [label="(10,4,0) Adding alloying elements increases constitutional supercooling ahead of solidification front"];
  "N21" [label="(12,4,0) Secondary phases can pin grain boundaries"];
  "N22" [label="(12,5,0) Secondary phases can break down epitaxial grain growth"];
  "N23" [label="(13,1,0) Additional elements may lead to formation of brittle intermetallics"];
  "N26" [label="(14,1,0) The mechanism by which phase transformation leads to grain refinement is not well understood"];
  "N27" [label="(14,2,0) Challenges exist in measuring and interpreting spatiotemporal evolution of microstructures and defects"];
  "N31" [label="(19,1,0) Increasing Mn content destabilizes the primary fcc phase during solidification"];
  "N32" [label="(19,2,0) Destabilizing primary fcc phase enables microstructure control in DED system"];
  "N33" [label="(19,3,0) In DED system, microstructure tends to be more columnar due to lower scanning speeds compared to PBF"];
  "N34" [label="(9,1,0) A deeper understanding of composition-driven process-structure-property relationships in MPEAs is needed"];
  "N35" [label="(9,2,0) Understanding composition-driven relationships will enable use of targeted compositions at specified locations"];
  "N36" [label="(9,3,0) Targeted compositions can enhance strength and performance of printed components"];
  "N5" [label="(5,1,0) Processing MPEAs via AM improves strength compared to conventional manufacturing"];
  "N7" [label="(6,1,0) AM processing of MPEAs presents challenges"];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) Investigate whether increasing Mn content in additively manufactured Fe80−xMnxCo10Cr10 multiprincipal element alloys destabilizes the primary fcc phase during directed energy deposition, induces phase transformations that interrupt columnar growth, and enables crack-free grain refinement, using thermodynamic modeling, operando X-ray diffraction, and multiscale microstructural characterization.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) When AM MPEAs show composition-sensitive phase behavior, columnar-grain challenges, and unclear transformation mechanisms, a cautious research aim is to test composition-driven strategies with modeling and characterization rather than to assert a solved mechanism."];
  "R12" [label="(0,0,0) Because DED microstructures tend to be more columnar and composition can alter AM microstructures, composition-based strategies are plausible to investigate for DED microstructure control."];
  "R14" [label="(0,0,0) Although secondary phases can refine grains, the possibility that added elements form brittle intermetallics motivates approaches that avoid brittle intermetallic formation."];
  "R15" [label="(0,0,0) The retained and repaired evidence motivates developing and evaluating a composition-driven approach for DED MPEAs in which Mn-related phase destabilization and characterization of microstructural evolution are used to understand and improve AM microstructure control."];
  "R3" [label="(0,0,0) Increasing Mn content can destabilize the primary fcc phase during solidification and thereby provides a route for microstructure control in the DED system."];
  "R7" [label="(0,0,0) AM processing of MPEAs is promising but still challenging, since it can improve strength while AM processing of MPEAs also presents challenges."];
  "R8" [label="(0,0,0) AM thermal conditions and composition are both relevant levers for altering or refining AM microstructures."];
